.TH DUMPDIR 1M 2/14/82
.UC 4
.SH NAME
dumpdir \- print the names of files and directories on a dump tape or disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dumpdir
[
.B f
filename ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Dumpdir
is used to read magtapes or disks dumped with the
.I dump
command 
.I Dumpdir
lists the names and inode numbers
of all the files and directories on the backup tape or disk.
.PP
The
.B f
option causes
.I filename
as the name of the dump device, whether tape or disk. 
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
dumpdir f /dev/xxxx
.PP
lists on the screen all the files and directories on the device
/dev/xxxx to which a file system has been dumped by the 
.IR dump (1M)
command.
.SH FILES
default backup unit varies with installation
.br
rst*
.SH "SEE ALSO"
dump(1M), restor(1M)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If the dump extends over more than one tape or disk,
it will ask you to change tapes or disks.
Reply with a new-line after the next one has been mounted.


